WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:10.877 --> 00:00:12.745
<i> REPORTER (over TV):
 Dian Fossey gained
 international fame</i>

00:00:12.845 --> 00:00:14.313 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> saving the last
 of the mountain gorillas...</i>

00:00:14.413 --> 00:00:16.149
<i> In connection with the death
 of naturalist Dian Fossey...</i>

00:00:16.249 --> 00:00:18.084
<i> Fossey has been found dead in
 the central African state...</i>

00:00:18.184 --> 00:00:20.786
<i> Fossey was found in her cabin
 in the African rainforest...</i>

00:00:20.886 --> 00:00:22.956
<i> Brutally murdered,
 hacked to death.</i>

00:00:25.558 --> 00:00:27.226 align:start size:88% position:13%
DIAN: I came here
essentially for research.

00:00:27.727 --> 00:00:30.697
I wanted to know all there
was to be known about them.

00:00:38.905 --> 00:00:41.741 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
<i> REPORTER (over TV): Dian
 knows their personalities,
 their habits and is learning</i>

00:00:41.841 --> 00:00:43.476 line:0%
<i> how they communicate.</i>

00:00:43.576 --> 00:00:45.945 line:0%
<i> Many who knew her saw a
 darker side, and felt she</i>

00:00:46.045 --> 00:00:48.314 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
<i> had become obsessed
 with saving the gorillas.</i>

00:00:48.581 --> 00:00:50.449 line:0%
DIAN: It was something I
just felt compelled to do.

00:00:50.549 --> 00:00:53.086 line:0%
I had to do it, I
can't explain it.

00:00:53.586 --> 00:00:55.655 line:0%
<i> REPORTER (over TV):
 Even if the police
 do solve her murder,</i>

00:00:55.755 --> 00:01:00.460 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
<i> another mystery will remain,
 the mystery of her life.</i>

00:01:14.974 --> 00:01:19.645
♪ ♪

00:01:19.745 --> 00:01:22.882 align:start size:84% position:16%
WAYNE: I always dreamed
of perhaps going
to Africa some day.

00:01:23.583 --> 00:01:27.787
I definitely wanted
to see scenery, I
wanted to see trees.

00:01:27.887 --> 00:01:30.423
I wanted the excitement.

00:01:40.867 --> 00:01:43.836 align:start size:88% position:13%
<i> CARSON (over TV): I think
 you're gonna find this
 discussion fascinating...</i>

00:01:43.936 --> 00:01:45.437 align:start size:78% position:22%
<i> I'm anxious to
 meet Dian Fossey...</i>

00:01:45.537 --> 00:01:47.774
WAYNE: Anybody who wanted
to study mountain gorillas,

00:01:47.874 --> 00:01:50.477 align:start size:94% position:6%
Dian Fossey was the
person you wanted to contact.

00:01:50.577 --> 00:01:52.111
She was famous.

00:01:52.211 --> 00:01:54.781 align:start size:84% position:16%
CARSON: Welcome please,
Dian Fossey.

00:01:58.718 --> 00:02:02.388 align:start size:91% position:9%
What prompted
you to go and choose this
particular area of animals?

00:02:03.789 --> 00:02:08.427 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was something I just felt
compelled to do, I had to
do it I can't explain it very

00:02:08.527 --> 00:02:14.200 align:start size:94% position:6%
dramatically it was
something I knew, there were
animals to be learned about

00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:16.703
and there weren't very many
gorillas left in the world.

00:02:16.803 --> 00:02:17.871
-Yeah.

00:02:17.971 --> 00:02:20.373 align:start size:78% position:22%
-There's certainly
a very few now.

00:02:20.473 --> 00:02:22.708 align:start size:91% position:9%
WAYNE: The only place
you could go if you wanted
to study gorillas was

00:02:22.808 --> 00:02:25.445
Karisoke Research
Centre in Rwanda.

00:02:27.146 --> 00:02:31.083
I was probably about
4 or 5 when I first
saw the gorillas at the

00:02:31.183 --> 00:02:36.923
Museum of Natural History
in New York City I felt
like the exhibit was alive,

00:02:41.660 --> 00:02:46.299 align:start size:97% position:3%
and I felt like I was stepping
into a world of nature
and it just, it fascinated me,

00:02:46.966 --> 00:02:49.302
it just overwhelmed
me with excitement.

00:02:50.837 --> 00:02:54.941 align:start position:0%
At that point I, I realized that
I want to see them some day.

00:02:55.508 --> 00:02:59.112 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then 30 years later
here I was studying mountain
gorillas with Dian Fossey.

00:03:06.752 --> 00:03:10.023
It was going to be
a dream come true.

00:03:12.425 --> 00:03:15.995
However, my dream come true
also became a nightmare.

00:03:30.610 --> 00:03:36.549 line:0%
♪ ♪

00:03:36.782 --> 00:03:42.021 align:start size:91% position:9%
It's so hard for me to talk
about this story, because
of the emotional pain.

00:03:45.024 --> 00:03:49.195
When I went into the room
it had tables knocked
over, papers everywhere.

00:04:03.542 --> 00:04:09.048 align:start size:91% position:9%
There was blood behind
her head, in her hair and a
gash going across her face

00:04:09.716 --> 00:04:13.385
over her nose,
on to her cheek.

00:04:13.652 --> 00:04:18.024
There was hair in her hand.

00:04:21.694 --> 00:04:23.629 align:start size:84% position:16%
I couldn't believe
what I was looking at.

00:04:23.729 --> 00:04:27.066 align:start size:94% position:6%
I couldn't believe that
she's lying there like that.

00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:31.170 align:start size:94% position:6%
Here's this woman that
always portrayed herself as
being strong and everything.

00:04:33.039 --> 00:04:35.341
Totally helpless
and totally gone.

00:04:44.750 --> 00:04:50.089 line:0%
♪ ♪

00:04:50.423 --> 00:04:54.059 align:start size:91% position:9%
SIGOURNEY: "There are
only 200 mountain gorillas
left in the world,

00:04:54.159 --> 00:04:58.097 align:start size:84% position:16%
which is why I
fight so hard for them.

00:05:01.367 --> 00:05:06.405 align:start size:94% position:6%
The man who kills
the animals today is the man
who kills the people who get

00:05:06.505 --> 00:05:08.775
in his way tomorrow."

00:05:10.676 --> 00:05:13.112
JOSEPH: I saw her body myself.

00:05:19.184 --> 00:05:23.055 align:start size:94% position:6%
She had been hacked to death
with a machete you know,
on her face on her head.

00:05:24.390 --> 00:05:29.295
Her eyes were open and
I kept thinking she's
alive but she was not.

00:05:30.529 --> 00:05:36.269
Uh it was really, um
it was very difficult.

00:05:44.343 --> 00:05:48.247
WATTS: Her last few moments
must have been really awful.

00:05:49.048 --> 00:05:51.784 line:0%
She would not have
died immediately.

00:05:51.884 --> 00:05:54.554 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
I'm sure she experienced
a lot of pain.

00:07:07.926 --> 00:07:12.265
-The clear implication
is these are the men
who got into her house.

00:07:12.365 --> 00:07:17.870 align:start size:94% position:6%
I never heard anything about
anyone trying to record
solid evidence of this

00:07:17.970 --> 00:07:19.872
trail of footprints.

00:07:51.637 --> 00:07:56.975 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
-I thought to myself
well you know, is that
her hair or is that maybe

00:07:57.309 --> 00:07:59.979 align:start size:91% position:9% line:0%
hair from the person or
persons that attacked her?

00:08:02.347 --> 00:08:07.953 align:start size:91% position:9%
I took hair out of her
right and left hand and put
them in separate envelopes.

00:08:09.021 --> 00:08:14.560
I cut hair off her head and
put that in an envelope so
it could be sent to the FBI.

00:08:16.528 --> 00:08:19.031
And the police did
see me doing that.

00:08:19.131 --> 00:08:21.700 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> REPORTER (over TV): A world
 renowned naturalist has
 been discovered murdered</i>

00:08:21.800 --> 00:08:23.436
<i> at her home in Africa.</i>

00:08:23.536 --> 00:08:26.605 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> Friends speculated
 that Dian Fossey, may have
 been murdered by poachers she</i>

00:08:26.705 --> 00:08:28.574 align:start size:78% position:22%
<i> had fought for
 the past 18 years.</i>

00:08:32.744 --> 00:08:37.249
IAN: For the outside world,
knowing, having read about
Dian's struggle against the

00:08:37.916 --> 00:08:41.587 line:0%
poachers, well it was
obvious, it was the
poachers what did it.

00:08:42.588 --> 00:08:45.191
But I don't think the
evidence stacks up.

00:08:47.927 --> 00:08:51.964 align:start size:91% position:9% line:0%
-I think it was
much more planned and
sophisticated than a thief

00:08:52.064 --> 00:08:54.066 line:0%
or a poacher going in.

00:09:00.940 --> 00:09:03.442
WAYNE: Something
didn't feel right.

00:09:04.410 --> 00:09:08.880 align:start size:97% position:3%
Everything that could
possibly be broken was broken,
like someone was

00:09:08.980 --> 00:09:11.216
in a rage, you know.

00:09:11.316 --> 00:09:13.618 align:start size:84% position:16%
Or someone was
looking for something.

00:09:14.553 --> 00:09:17.156 line:0%
-Drawers were pulled open,
things had been pulled out.

00:09:19.025 --> 00:09:21.994 align:start size:91% position:9%
It looked like somebody
was looking for something.

00:09:22.495 --> 00:09:23.929
Money was not taken.

00:09:24.030 --> 00:09:26.632
There was a couple of
hand guns down there.

00:09:27.432 --> 00:09:31.938
When you don't take the money,
when you don't take the gun,
when you don't take anything

00:09:32.038 --> 00:09:36.442 align:start size:91% position:9%
visible, to me that
automatically excludes
poachers being the people.

00:09:39.845 --> 00:09:44.550 align:start size:91% position:9%
It looks like a set up,
it looked like it was done
to just make believe that

00:09:45.351 --> 00:09:47.486
poachers have done that.

00:09:52.558 --> 00:09:56.195 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
JOHN: Whoever came here
that night cut a hole through
this corrugated iron with

00:09:56.295 --> 00:10:00.499 line:0%
a machete like this, called
a panga, then crawled inside
and slashed her to death.

00:10:05.037 --> 00:10:11.477 align:start position:0%
-Someone cut a small piece,
3 by 3 feet hole in the bedroom.

00:10:16.381 --> 00:10:18.617
-That's gonna make noise.

00:10:18.717 --> 00:10:21.286
So why wouldn't she flee?

00:10:21.386 --> 00:10:25.224 align:start size:97% position:3%
How did she end up being
killed right there by her bed?

00:10:27.826 --> 00:10:32.230 align:start size:94% position:6%
-The official story was,
whoever did that did it from
the outside and got into the

00:10:32.330 --> 00:10:35.033
house by doing that.

00:10:35.400 --> 00:10:40.539 align:start size:88% position:13%
But I think it's probably
a lot more likely
that whoever did it,

00:10:40.639 --> 00:10:45.911
did it from the inside to
make it look like that's
how they had gotten in.

00:10:48.847 --> 00:10:51.750
-It almost seemed
like it was staged.

00:10:52.017 --> 00:10:55.487
The amazing thing about
it was there wasn't a
heck of a lot of blood.

00:10:55.587 --> 00:10:57.156
You know, I'm wondering,
'What's going on here?

00:10:57.256 --> 00:11:01.360 align:start size:94% position:6%
If you got slashed
with a machete you should be
bleeding all over the place'.

00:11:03.028 --> 00:11:06.532 align:start size:88% position:13%
-Was she killed someplace
else and brought
back into the room?

00:11:10.336 --> 00:11:13.873 align:start size:84% position:16%
-From what I saw
nothing comes together
in to a coherent story.

00:11:21.547 --> 00:11:24.617
-It may have been a killing
that was ordered by someone.

00:11:43.068 --> 00:11:48.474 line:0%
♪ ♪

00:11:50.042 --> 00:11:54.312 align:start position:0%
SIGOURNEY:
"When contemplating the vast
expanse of uninhabited, rugged,

00:11:54.413 --> 00:11:59.451 align:start size:88% position:13%
mountainous land
surrounding me I consider
myself one of the world's

00:11:59.551 --> 00:12:02.088
most fortunate people."

00:12:07.826 --> 00:12:11.697 align:start size:94% position:6%
There are no words to
describe the joy and complete
satisfaction one feels,

00:12:12.464 --> 00:12:17.103 align:start size:94% position:6%
after sitting in their
midst for several hours in
mutual trust and confidence.

00:12:19.638 --> 00:12:23.676
At times the rapport
simply overwhelms me.

00:12:24.810 --> 00:12:28.314 align:start size:81% position:19%
It is the only
place that I belong.

00:12:36.522 --> 00:12:38.757 align:start size:88% position:13%
<i> REPORTER (over TV): High
 on the hills of Rwanda
 in Central Africa,</i>

00:12:38.858 --> 00:12:43.095
<i> Dian Fossey was buried today.</i>

00:12:43.195 --> 00:12:48.801 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> She was buried according to
 her wishes, among the animals
 that never harmed her.</i>

00:12:51.737 --> 00:12:55.841
IAN: She was buried
8 years to the day
since Digit's death.

00:13:09.922 --> 00:13:14.660 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
-Whatever happened
to her she didn't deserve
being brutally killed and

00:13:16.294 --> 00:13:18.631 line:0%
stowed away in the ground.

00:13:26.138 --> 00:13:28.807
WAYNE: It was almost
like it was surreal.

00:13:29.475 --> 00:13:31.643 align:start size:81% position:19%
I will never talk
to this woman again.

00:13:31.744 --> 00:13:34.446
I will never see
her alive again.

00:13:43.455 --> 00:13:48.127 line:0%
♪ ♪

00:13:54.333 --> 00:13:59.205 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
-She was a prominent person,
and she had been murdered,
in a brutal fashion.

00:14:01.506 --> 00:14:06.111 align:start size:94% position:6%
The Rwandan's obviously were
embarrassed that this crime
had occurred and probably

00:14:06.211 --> 00:14:10.149
worried that it was gonna
bring negative publicity.

00:14:18.490 --> 00:14:22.428 align:start size:84% position:16%
-I was now in
a situation where I was
in charge of this camp.

00:14:24.396 --> 00:14:29.835 align:start size:94% position:6%
Soon after the funeral,
a day or two later I got
someone knocking on my door,

00:14:30.269 --> 00:14:35.441 align:start size:97% position:3%
looked like he might be
police or military and he said
"I'm taking these guys down,

00:14:36.875 --> 00:14:38.677
I hope you understand."

00:14:56.628 --> 00:15:01.100 align:start size:91% position:9%
-They took away several of
the most important trackers
to be interrogated.

00:15:04.536 --> 00:15:08.173
-It clearly, as far as
we could tell was not
staff who killed Dian.

00:15:10.008 --> 00:15:14.446
IAN: If you've had a job
for nearly 20 years do
you kill your boss and,

00:15:15.180 --> 00:15:18.217
and be out of work?

00:15:25.724 --> 00:15:30.863 align:start size:97% position:3%
I was asked to go and
deal with her belongings and
assess the future of the camp.

00:15:32.397 --> 00:15:35.901
And I went up to Karisoke
with the American Consul.

00:15:38.003 --> 00:15:42.408 align:start size:91% position:9%
-The embassy had taken
possession of the property
pending an inventory

00:15:43.041 --> 00:15:45.376
of her effects

00:15:46.244 --> 00:15:50.649 align:start size:94% position:6%
-For me the most
significant thing was looking
through a letter file,

00:15:50.749 --> 00:15:54.920
I found a letter, a carbon
copy of a letter, to me,
that I'd never received.

00:15:59.424 --> 00:16:01.827 line:0%
SIGOURNEY: "Dear Ian...

00:16:03.928 --> 00:16:07.967 align:start size:91% position:9%
The latest poacher captured
is also a gold smuggler
between Zaire and Rwanda.

00:16:10.836 --> 00:16:15.908
I examined his clothing to
find a letter between him
and his dealer setting up

00:16:16.008 --> 00:16:17.976
appointment places
for gold deliveries."

00:16:19.778 --> 00:16:24.416 align:start size:97% position:3%
-It might have got lost in the
post, but it's odd that all
the other carbon copies of the

00:16:24.516 --> 00:16:28.187
letters were letters
that I'd received but
this one, was missing.

00:16:31.123 --> 00:16:32.424
Gold smuggling...

00:16:32.524 --> 00:16:34.359
that's serious people.

00:16:34.459 --> 00:16:38.663
People with money and if their
names are on a piece of paper
that's evidence against them.

00:16:40.365 --> 00:16:45.838
-Reading that with Ian felt
very much like we were the,
that we were understanding

00:16:47.339 --> 00:16:50.876 align:start size:88% position:13%
exactly what had happened
there at that moment.

00:16:52.711 --> 00:16:56.048
-There was always smuggling
going on through the park
that was a well-known fact.

00:16:58.484 --> 00:17:03.421
-Dian quite often made it
known to people that she
had information on them,

00:17:04.289 --> 00:17:06.992
so they better watch
their "Ps and Qs".

00:17:07.092 --> 00:17:10.929
-The carbon copy of the
letter seemed to me to
be important evidence,

00:17:11.296 --> 00:17:14.566
so I photocopied it and gave
a copy to the authorities.

00:17:21.406 --> 00:17:25.043 line:0%
-The day after I got back
there was a knock on the
Embassy door and the police

00:17:25.443 --> 00:17:28.246
were there and they said they
would like the hair samples.

00:17:28.813 --> 00:17:30.515
So I divided them up.

00:17:30.615 --> 00:17:33.652
So they got half the
hair samples and I kept
half the hair samples.

00:17:55.173 --> 00:17:57.041
WATTS: We were all suspects.

00:17:57.142 --> 00:18:01.146
Anybody, any outsider or
any foreigner they can
connect with Karisoke,

00:18:01.679 --> 00:18:06.651 align:start size:94% position:6%
so we thought it's all
kind of absurd, but it's
not impossible that something

00:18:06.751 --> 00:18:09.088
bad could happen

00:18:16.261 --> 00:18:21.333 align:start size:94% position:6%
-One day I had
found a skeleton of a gorilla
and I brought the pieces back

00:18:22.267 --> 00:18:27.005 align:start size:88% position:13%
to camp and put them
on the picnic table that
was near Dian's house and

00:18:27.105 --> 00:18:29.441
so I was examining it.

00:18:30.208 --> 00:18:33.512 align:start size:94% position:6%
I noticed as I looked up
there was somebody in there.

00:18:33.612 --> 00:18:36.782 align:start size:84% position:16%
I could see them,
just kind of a shadow.

00:18:38.617 --> 00:18:43.087 align:start size:91% position:9%
I got concerned, so my
first response feeling I'm
responsible for the camp,

00:18:43.187 --> 00:18:48.760 align:start size:94% position:6%
was to go over to
the window and to look in,
and actually probably wasn't

00:18:48.860 --> 00:18:52.030
the smartest thing to do
but I went into the cabin.

00:19:03.475 --> 00:19:08.313
-When I did, no sooner did
I do that, I turned around
there was a guard coming up.

00:19:13.719 --> 00:19:16.522
WAYNE: I didn't have boxes.
I wasn't stealing anything.

00:19:21.727 --> 00:19:23.795
-The event kind of
got out of hand.

00:19:24.463 --> 00:19:26.030
I went back to my house.

00:19:26.130 --> 00:19:30.034
There was a hot head there
with a gun and he started
yelling and screaming at me

00:19:30.134 --> 00:19:32.471
and he took a rifle
like to aim at me.

00:19:40.245 --> 00:19:42.848
-There was nothing
for me to gain by
going into the house.

00:19:43.881 --> 00:19:45.884
What did I need?

00:19:45.984 --> 00:19:48.387
It's a mistake I made.

00:19:50.755 --> 00:19:54.993 align:start size:88% position:13%
-Breaking into the
house of Dian Fossey,
stealing some of Dian's,

00:19:55.093 --> 00:19:57.829
manuscripts or something.

00:19:58.096 --> 00:20:02.701
If it's true, and he did that
and they have evidence then
I would be suspicious of Wayne.

00:20:05.570 --> 00:20:08.273 align:start size:97% position:3%
WAYNE: The next thing you know
I was accused of murder.

00:20:21.686 --> 00:20:25.424 align:start size:91% position:9%
WAYNE: I received a
letter that I needed to go
down to the police station

00:20:26.091 --> 00:20:28.459
for a questioning.

00:20:29.394 --> 00:20:32.864 align:start size:94% position:6%
The Prosecutor came in after
everybody else was there.

00:20:32.965 --> 00:20:36.201
He came in and he would
pace back and forth like
this and look at me.

00:20:36.301 --> 00:20:38.803
'Why didn't you hear all the
noise when she was murdered?'

00:20:39.204 --> 00:20:41.472
'I was sleeping sound asleep,
I was the other side of camp'.

00:20:42.206 --> 00:20:43.875 align:start size:81% position:19%
'Who would have
killed Dian Fossey?'

00:20:43.975 --> 00:20:45.610 align:start size:81% position:19%
'Who would have
killed Dian Fossey?'

00:20:45.710 --> 00:20:51.283 align:start size:91% position:9%
I said 'poachers' and
he kept turning around and
saying, 'No you killed her.

00:20:52.317 --> 00:20:55.687 align:start size:91% position:9%
You broke in and you stole
her precious documents,
you killed her for

00:20:55.787 --> 00:20:57.689
her precious documents'.

00:20:57.789 --> 00:20:59.490
'What?

00:20:59.591 --> 00:21:03.561
I didn't kill her, we were
friends' and every once in a
while the guy behind me would

00:21:03.662 --> 00:21:06.264 align:start size:88% position:13%
push my shoulder like
this, pushing me forward.

00:21:06.364 --> 00:21:10.702
So I've got a prosecutor here,
I've got an interpreter over
here and someone behind me and

00:21:10.802 --> 00:21:15.673
so I was boxed in.

00:21:15.773 --> 00:21:18.677
I'm by myself and I'm trapped.

00:21:18.910 --> 00:21:22.647 align:start size:88% position:13%
He would make
an accusation and push,
make an accusation, push,

00:21:22.747 --> 00:21:26.785
he kept raising his voice,
kept raising his voice, over
and over and over again,

00:21:26.885 --> 00:21:28.987
louder and louder
and push, push.

00:21:29.087 --> 00:21:31.957
I kept saying 'I didn't
do it, I didn't do this'.

00:21:32.057 --> 00:21:35.861
He pushed this paper
towards me with a
pen 'sign the paper'.

00:21:38.730 --> 00:21:41.466 align:start size:88% position:13%
'I didn't kill anybody',
'Sign it, sign it.'

00:21:41.733 --> 00:21:43.068 align:start size:78% position:22%
'I don't want
to sign any paper,

00:21:43.168 --> 00:21:45.704
I didn't do anything'.

00:21:48.406 --> 00:21:51.676
'You just need to calm down,
relax and sign that paper'.

00:21:51.943 --> 00:21:55.012 align:start size:84% position:16%
And the way he said
it, it seemed like I
was in a bad situation,

00:21:55.112 --> 00:21:57.982
that if I didn't do
it, something else
was gonna happen.

00:21:58.082 --> 00:22:01.986
There's nobody else here,
just me, the prosecutor and
these other two gentlemen.

00:22:02.086 --> 00:22:05.390 align:start size:81% position:19%
There's no witnesses,
there's nothing.

00:22:05.490 --> 00:22:07.759
I feared for my life.

00:22:11.195 --> 00:22:13.965
So I signed it
and that was it.

00:22:18.503 --> 00:22:22.207
Then I went back to camp.

00:22:25.043 --> 00:22:28.513
Months go by and everything
seemed to go back to normal.

00:22:30.681 --> 00:22:34.119
WATTS: During the murder
investigation everyone who
worked at Karisoke had been

00:22:35.853 --> 00:22:39.524 align:start size:91% position:9%
interrogated but then they
were released with the
exception of Rwelekana.

00:22:43.695 --> 00:22:46.965 align:start size:84% position:16%
JOSEPH: He used
to be one of the best
tracker of Dian Fossey.

00:22:48.533 --> 00:22:51.035 align:start size:84% position:16%
AMY: He had quit
Karisoke several times.

00:22:51.870 --> 00:22:56.975 align:start size:88% position:13%
IAN: Dian's relationship
with her employees
was often very volatile.

00:23:00.412 --> 00:23:04.716 align:start size:91% position:9%
-She would mistreat
people who displeased her.

00:23:08.320 --> 00:23:13.157 align:start size:94% position:6%
She'd tell someone summarily
you're fired get out of camp,
then whatever was usually

00:23:13.258 --> 00:23:17.362
would blow over, she'd forget
about it and the next time
they were due to come up for

00:23:17.462 --> 00:23:20.665 align:start size:94% position:6%
their shift they were
allowed to come back to work.

00:23:22.801 --> 00:23:26.137 align:start size:81% position:19%
-She was the kind
of boss that everyone
hopes they don't get.

00:23:26.805 --> 00:23:32.511 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Rwelekana was more
prideful than others and
sometimes would counter Dian

00:23:33.311 --> 00:23:35.513
with what she said.

00:23:35.847 --> 00:23:40.151 align:start size:97% position:3%
And he would say 'Okay I'm
not taking this, I, you know
I'm leaving' and then he'd get

00:23:40.251 --> 00:23:43.454
re-hired cos he was great.

00:23:43.988 --> 00:23:46.925
-The day Dian died
he was not there.

00:24:17.121 --> 00:24:22.227 align:start size:88% position:13%
-He left and it was
his decision and
that got distorted into,

00:24:23.127 --> 00:24:26.998 align:start size:97% position:3%
'No he wanted to go on working
there, she didn't want him,

00:24:27.098 --> 00:24:29.468 align:start size:81% position:19%
she fired him
that made him angry'

00:24:36.273 --> 00:24:41.145 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Our understanding was,
at that time in the country,
the way illegal acts were

00:24:41.612 --> 00:24:44.816 align:start size:91% position:9%
investigated was
through interrogation, not
through physical evidence.

00:24:53.157 --> 00:24:57.062
KARL: The Rwandan's were out
of their investigative depth.

00:24:58.829 --> 00:25:02.734
It was escalating in anxiety
as a, irritant between us.

00:25:08.706 --> 00:25:12.577
-The camp staff said
two sets of footprints
came up to the cabin.

00:25:15.079 --> 00:25:18.884 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Those were two men who were
in camp that night who were
not supposed to be there.

00:25:58.722 --> 00:26:03.461 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We began to get word
in the embassy that um, that
the investigation was coming

00:26:04.595 --> 00:26:06.797
to a conclusion.

00:26:07.431 --> 00:26:12.603
-'Good news we've found the
culprit, we've found the
guilty party in the case of

00:26:12.704 --> 00:26:16.107
the Dian Fossey murder
and it is Wayne McGuire'.

00:26:18.509 --> 00:26:23.081
-The Embassy just said they
were charging me with the
murder of Dian Fossey, and

00:26:23.181 --> 00:26:27.351 align:start size:91% position:9%
I have to admit at that
point I kind of went blank.

00:26:28.052 --> 00:26:31.956 align:start size:88% position:13%
-The authorities said
that Wayne and Rwelekana,
had conspired together to

00:26:32.056 --> 00:26:33.958
cook up a murder plot.

00:26:34.058 --> 00:26:36.360
It doesn't make sense.

00:26:37.061 --> 00:26:39.997
-Wayne couldn't speak French
Kinyarwandan or Ki-Swahili.

00:26:40.698 --> 00:26:42.767 align:start size:78% position:22%
Rwelekana couldn't
speak English.

00:26:42.867 --> 00:26:45.269
WAYNE: The gentleman
that was arrested?

00:26:45.369 --> 00:26:49.074 align:start size:88% position:13%
I never met him
in my entire life, so
I have no clue who he is

00:26:53.912 --> 00:26:57.148
-The best thing we could do
for his safety and security

00:26:57.248 --> 00:26:59.718 align:start size:78% position:22%
was to get him
out of the country.

00:27:01.552 --> 00:27:05.189 align:start size:91% position:9%
-All of a sudden the
adrenaline started pumping
and my only concern was,

00:27:05.290 --> 00:27:07.892
how am I going to get
out of this situation?

00:27:08.893 --> 00:27:12.396
I remember getting on the
plane and was terrified.

00:27:12.496 --> 00:27:15.967
And I, and I was in First
Class, that's all my
mother could get for me,

00:27:16.067 --> 00:27:20.905
and I was in there with the,
the World Bank people and they
had a champagne bottle about

00:27:21.005 --> 00:27:25.376 align:start size:97% position:3%
four feet high and popping
it, drinking champagne and I'm
sitting there terrified, like,

00:27:25.476 --> 00:27:28.846
'Am I gonna get out of here?'

00:27:29.513 --> 00:27:33.251
Any time someone could just
pull over and arrest me.

00:27:43.428 --> 00:27:46.097
-I think he was very lucky.

00:27:48.666 --> 00:27:51.236 align:start position:0%
<i>REPORTER (over TV): The
hunt is on this morning for an
American wildlife researcher,</i>

00:27:51.336 --> 00:27:54.872 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> Wayne McGuire as the prime
 suspect in the murder
 of naturalist Dian Fossey.</i>

00:27:55.673 --> 00:27:57.275 align:start size:78% position:22%
<i> McGuire left the
 country last month.</i>

00:27:57.375 --> 00:27:59.910
<i> His whereabouts unknown.</i>

00:28:00.010 --> 00:28:04.015 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> Rwandan Police have asked
 international authorities
 for help in locating McGuire.</i>

00:28:18.363 --> 00:28:22.033
WAYNE: I want to respond
to the outrageous charge
of the Rwandan government

00:28:22.934 --> 00:28:25.937
that I murdered
Dr. Dian Fossey.

00:28:26.037 --> 00:28:29.574 align:start size:81% position:19%
I had absolutely
nothing to do with
Dian's tragic death.

00:28:29.674 --> 00:28:32.710
She was my friend and
one of my mentors.

00:28:33.143 --> 00:28:36.614
I had everything to lose and
nothing to gain by her death.

00:28:36.714 --> 00:28:40.184
I am shocked and outraged
at these false allegations.

00:28:40.284 --> 00:28:43.988 align:start size:84% position:16%
The Justice Department
is free to question
me at any time.

00:28:44.288 --> 00:28:47.091 align:start size:81% position:19%
-The Rwandans had
solved their problem.

00:28:47.658 --> 00:28:52.630
They had identified who had
killed the prominent American

00:28:54.165 --> 00:28:56.200
and the American embassy had

00:28:56.301 --> 00:28:59.870 align:start size:88% position:13%
spirited that person
out of the country and
so therefore the Rwandans

00:28:59.970 --> 00:29:02.340
had done their job.

00:29:12.317 --> 00:29:16.354 align:start size:91% position:9%
-Wayne McGuire didn't
strike me as someone who
was hiding a guilty secret.

00:29:20.825 --> 00:29:24.429 align:start size:94% position:6%
-There certainly seemed
nothing unusual about Wayne.

00:29:27.565 --> 00:29:31.369 align:start size:88% position:13%
-When I think about
Wayne knowing him, Wayne
killing someone, hmm.

00:29:33.638 --> 00:29:36.775
The question is why would
Wayne kill Dian Fossey?

00:29:39.610 --> 00:29:42.580 align:start size:91% position:9%
-I want to make this
clear, I did not kill Dian.

00:29:56.294 --> 00:29:59.130 line:0%
♪ ♪

00:30:06.070 --> 00:30:10.208 align:start size:97% position:3%
-We heard that
Rwelekana had died, in prison,

00:30:11.643 --> 00:30:14.879
and the official story was that

00:30:14.979 --> 00:30:18.049 align:start size:81% position:19%
he had hung
himself in his cell.

00:30:18.149 --> 00:30:21.786
They said that shows
that he was guilty.

00:31:11.268 --> 00:31:13.270
JOSEPH: He was
a very nice man.

00:31:13.771 --> 00:31:16.407 align:start size:91% position:9%
AMY: He was a great friend,
he was a family man.

00:31:16.774 --> 00:31:19.277
Just a man of real integrity.

00:31:23.781 --> 00:31:26.618 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was convenient to go
after him and, and kill him.

00:31:27.885 --> 00:31:30.555
And it was terrible.

00:31:55.113 --> 00:31:58.181
<i> REPORTER (over TV): McGuire
 was tried in his absence
 and convicted with a Rwandan</i>

00:31:58.282 --> 00:32:02.353 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> co-worker who allegedly
 committed suicide in his
 prison cell before the trial.</i>

00:32:04.888 --> 00:32:06.991
KARL: I did attend the trial.

00:32:07.224 --> 00:32:10.261 align:start size:91% position:9%
Any reasonable person
would have found that there
was no compelling evidence

00:32:10.361 --> 00:32:12.429
whatsoever, it was farcical.

00:32:12.529 --> 00:32:15.332 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> REPORTER (over TV): At the
 trial no defense lawyer
 appeared for McGuire,</i>

00:32:15.899 --> 00:32:17.267
<i> no witnesses were called.</i>

00:32:17.367 --> 00:32:19.436 align:start size:81% position:19%
<i> No physical evidence
 was presented.</i>

00:32:19.536 --> 00:32:22.173
<i> The trial lasted 30 minutes.</i>

00:32:25.576 --> 00:32:31.916 align:start size:91% position:9%
-A judgment was rendered
of guilty as charged
and a sentence of death was

00:32:32.016 --> 00:32:34.652
handed down for Wayne McGuire.

00:32:35.886 --> 00:32:38.256
KATHLEEN: I thought it was
ridiculous and it was wrong.

00:32:38.923 --> 00:32:43.695
They had no real evidence of
his guilt, none whatsoever.

00:32:47.998 --> 00:32:50.768
JUVENS: As a Rwandan
it makes me feel bad.

00:32:53.871 --> 00:32:57.442 align:start size:97% position:3%
Today, if I saw a judgment
like this, I would be shocked.

00:32:58.709 --> 00:33:01.446
I would say the judge is
incompetent beyond belief.

00:33:04.182 --> 00:33:07.819
IAN: Those who charged
him suggested he wanted
to steal her research.

00:33:10.688 --> 00:33:12.957 align:start size:97% position:3%
-That's the word that
popped up over and over again,

00:33:13.057 --> 00:33:15.493
'precious documents,
precious documents.'

00:33:16.994 --> 00:33:20.764 align:start size:81% position:19% line:0%
-You had to be as
out of touch as that
government of Rwanda,

00:33:20.865 --> 00:33:24.268 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
to think that you could
kill the most famous
person in a field,

00:33:24.368 --> 00:33:28.373
take their information
and publish it and
become famous yourself.

00:33:34.178 --> 00:33:37.214 align:start size:88% position:13%
-They made the accusation
that it was my hair.

00:33:38.549 --> 00:33:42.286 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> REPORTER (over TV): The
 prosecutor explained to CNN
 strands of hair found in Miss</i>

00:33:42.386 --> 00:33:45.622
<i> Fossey's hand were sent to
 a lab in Paris for analysis.</i>

00:33:46.857 --> 00:33:50.828 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> The lab confirmed the hairs
 were those of a white person
 other than Ms. Fossey.</i>

00:33:51.562 --> 00:33:55.666
<i> McGuire was the only other
 white person in the area
 on the night of the murder.</i>

00:34:02.506 --> 00:34:07.978
-From reading the forensic
reports established in Paris
it is obvious that they did

00:34:08.378 --> 00:34:13.517 align:start size:94% position:6%
not take any samples from
Wayne to compare it with the
samples they found in the

00:34:13.617 --> 00:34:15.686
hands of the victim.

00:34:15.786 --> 00:34:20.458 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, how can this be
incontestable, I don't know?

00:34:23.995 --> 00:34:28.465
-If the report says she had
her own hair in one hand and
somebody else's hair in the

00:34:28.565 --> 00:34:33.204
other hand, why didn't they
test Wayne McGuire's hair?

00:34:35.572 --> 00:34:38.476 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It could have been her hair
because it was dark hair.

00:34:38.576 --> 00:34:43.748
AMY: She could have just
reached up when she got hit
and grabbed her own hair,

00:34:43.848 --> 00:34:47.051
which would be a
logical reaction.

00:34:47.151 --> 00:34:51.155
-I got back a very, um,
non answer from the FBI.

00:34:54.859 --> 00:34:59.430 align:start size:88% position:13%
It was inconclusive as to
whether or not the hair,
in her hands was the

00:34:59.530 --> 00:35:02.033
hair on her head.

00:35:02.333 --> 00:35:04.802 align:start size:91% position:9%
-It wouldn't be conclusive
proof either way.

00:35:04.902 --> 00:35:08.238 align:start size:94% position:6%
We know that the crime
scene's contaminated by
lots of people moving about.

00:35:09.606 --> 00:35:12.443 align:start size:91% position:9%
-The Americans said to
the Rwandans, 'You've got
to find out who did this',

00:35:13.877 --> 00:35:16.881
and so the Rwandans "did".

00:35:18.015 --> 00:35:22.920 align:start size:94% position:6%
-The Rwandan authorities
either were truly incompetent
or they didn't want

00:35:24.588 --> 00:35:27.592
to solve the crime.

00:35:37.868 --> 00:35:42.139 align:start size:91% position:9%
-Wayne McGuire and
Rwelekana, in my view, were
not the guilty culprits.

00:35:43.406 --> 00:35:46.677 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't think you can
draw any conclusions from
the fact that the footprints

00:35:46.777 --> 00:35:48.779
went by Wayne's cabin.

00:35:48.879 --> 00:35:52.549 align:start size:94% position:6%
The path that's most
likely to get you to Dian's
cabin without being heard is

00:35:52.649 --> 00:35:55.653
the one that goes
by Wayne's cabin.

00:35:56.987 --> 00:35:59.423
Dian's murder is
still unsolved.

00:36:02.859 --> 00:36:05.962
-I didn't believe
the official story.

00:36:06.063 --> 00:36:10.634
-It just seemed the Rwandan
government was happy to have
Wayne out of the country and

00:36:10.735 --> 00:36:13.871
Rwelekana dead and the
case could be closed.

00:36:17.875 --> 00:36:21.479 align:start size:94% position:6%
FRANK: She had almost
continuous difficulties with
one or another element of the

00:36:22.212 --> 00:36:24.215
Rwandan government.

00:36:24.315 --> 00:36:28.920 align:start size:97% position:3%
-She was becoming an obstacle.
-A thorn in their sides.
-She knew she had enemies.

00:36:30.588 --> 00:36:34.592 align:start size:84% position:16%
-If the government
wanted Dian Fossey
out of Rwanda they had

00:36:36.026 --> 00:36:39.597
the power to just get her out.

00:36:41.265 --> 00:36:43.901
-I keep going back to
the gold smuggling.

00:36:45.102 --> 00:36:51.409
-I think someone in a high
position suspected, or knew,
that she had something on him

00:36:52.109 --> 00:36:53.844
and had her killed.

00:36:53.944 --> 00:36:57.348
-They certainly could
have found somebody
around who would do it.

00:37:00.684 --> 00:37:05.556 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Dian's letter suggests
that she had uncovered an
illegal gold smuggling ring,

00:37:06.690 --> 00:37:10.061 align:start size:84% position:16%
and that someone in
a position of authority
was implicated in that.

00:37:14.031 --> 00:37:18.135
-I think it's possible
that an official could
have had her killed,

00:37:20.337 --> 00:37:23.507
because she knew things.

00:37:26.110 --> 00:37:30.214
-Dian had signed a contract
for a movie of her life.

00:37:32.049 --> 00:37:36.520 align:start size:91% position:9%
-The film deal that
she was negotiating for the
book<i> Gorilla's in the Mist.</i>

00:37:38.389 --> 00:37:42.793
-She talked about having
evidence that she was going
to disclose to the world.

00:37:47.631 --> 00:37:53.871
-People involved in illegal
activities might be afraid of
a global spotlight being put

00:37:53.971 --> 00:37:56.707
on them by a Hollywood movie.

00:37:58.542 --> 00:38:03.547 align:start size:97% position:3%
There were perhaps some
very powerful forces at play,
trying to silence Dian Fossey.

00:38:08.452 --> 00:38:12.423
(explosions)

00:38:22.933 --> 00:38:26.603 align:start size:91% position:9%
-Many people were massacred
during the genocide.

00:38:26.837 --> 00:38:30.107
Others just fled the country.

00:38:30.841 --> 00:38:35.313 align:start size:97% position:3%
The entire court the Ruhengeri
court was burnt down.

00:38:36.981 --> 00:38:41.819
Chances of getting any
documentation anything
related to the trial is,

00:38:44.154 --> 00:38:47.190
is almost impossible.

00:38:48.692 --> 00:38:54.565
-Whoever is responsible is
either walking free or has,
has perished in the wider

00:38:54.665 --> 00:38:58.035 align:start size:88% position:13%
bloodshed that Rwanda
experienced in the 90's.

00:39:01.538 --> 00:39:04.674
-I don't think
we'll ever know.

00:39:04.775 --> 00:39:09.246
But I don't think that Dian
would have objected to that
as an ending for the script,

00:39:10.614 --> 00:39:15.052
because she died a warrior,
she would have written that.

00:39:27.931 --> 00:39:32.803 line:0%
♪ ♪

00:39:33.471 --> 00:39:36.006
-It's a tragedy on all sides.

00:39:36.106 --> 00:39:37.374
Dian lost her life.

00:39:37.474 --> 00:39:39.877
Rwelekana lost his.

00:39:39.977 --> 00:39:43.280
And Wayne's life
was hugely changed.

00:39:46.283 --> 00:39:48.586
IAN: Wayne had to
change his career.

00:39:54.325 --> 00:39:58.662 align:start size:94% position:6%
WAYNE: Losing my academic
career, what I had dreamed of
since I was 5 years old was

00:39:58.762 --> 00:40:03.167
more severe than being accused
of murder believe it or not.

00:40:06.636 --> 00:40:12.242
-Obviously the Rwanda of today
is a different place and there
would be an expectation of a

00:40:13.243 --> 00:40:18.416 align:start size:94% position:6%
much more, I think, fair
and modern judicial process.

00:40:23.687 --> 00:40:29.026
-The damage is done, you know,
to clear my name would be
nice but to live for that one

00:40:29.526 --> 00:40:33.764
simple moment, no that's
not worth that, that's
not what I'm looking for.

00:40:35.365 --> 00:40:39.169 align:start size:88% position:13%
I'm in a different
field now, I work in the
field of mental health,

00:40:39.269 --> 00:40:42.439
helping people to recover.

00:40:42.539 --> 00:40:45.843 align:start size:84% position:16%
I am able to help other
people because I've
experienced trauma.

00:40:55.552 --> 00:40:59.123 line:0%
♪ ♪

00:41:06.197 --> 00:41:08.532 align:start size:84% position:16%
FELIX: Dian's story
was a story of courage.

00:41:12.802 --> 00:41:14.538
The gorillas are thriving.

00:41:14.638 --> 00:41:17.441 align:start size:97% position:3%
The numbers have doubled
since the time of Dian Fossey.

00:41:23.713 --> 00:41:27.985 align:start size:94% position:6%
If Dian hadn't come to
Rwanda to habituate gorillas,
to study their behavior,

00:41:28.952 --> 00:41:31.956
they would not be here today.

00:41:42.299 --> 00:41:44.902 align:start size:91% position:9% line:0%
-If anybody could say that
they'd saved a species,

00:41:45.336 --> 00:41:47.637 line:0%
I would think that Dian could.

00:41:47.738 --> 00:41:52.843 align:start size:84% position:16%
She undoubtedly turned
the world's attention
towards gorillas.

00:41:54.344 --> 00:41:59.316 align:start size:94% position:6%
-She somehow got behind the
big, bluff bravado and found
the real gorilla.

00:42:00.750 --> 00:42:05.489 align:start size:84% position:16%
It's that amazing
meeting of another
mind that happens to be

00:42:06.089 --> 00:42:09.326 align:start size:84% position:16%
in a non-human
body that is the magic

00:42:09.893 --> 00:42:12.296
and that's what Dian
opened up to the world.

00:42:12.596 --> 00:42:14.831
(making gorilla noises).

00:42:15.465 --> 00:42:17.902
BETTIE: You had to learn
how to make gorilla sounds.

00:42:19.269 --> 00:42:25.208
(making gorilla noises).

00:42:25.509 --> 00:42:27.411
-They like that huh?

00:42:30.113 --> 00:42:34.017 align:start size:91% position:9%
-The work that she
started, the innovations
that she brought, you know,

00:42:34.117 --> 00:42:40.290
habituating gorillas, getting
to know them individually
and starting what she called

00:42:40.957 --> 00:42:44.261
active conservation is
still what we do today.

00:42:47.263 --> 00:42:51.935 align:start size:94% position:6%
-The first gorillas
she contacted in 67, the
descendants of those animals

00:42:52.035 --> 00:42:55.873 align:start size:94% position:6%
are still being followed,
monitored and observed today.

00:43:03.780 --> 00:43:08.719
-Gorilla tourism went from
being a potential threat
to the gorillas to being an

00:43:08.819 --> 00:43:11.722
important part of the
saving of the gorillas.

00:43:15.392 --> 00:43:20.797 align:start size:94% position:6%
Before she died Dian somewhat
reluctantly admitted publicly
that the way it was being

00:43:21.198 --> 00:43:24.301 align:start size:94% position:6%
managed, gorilla tourism was
changing things for good.

00:43:27.070 --> 00:43:31.675
-It has taken a huge effort
from everyone, from the
Government from the partners

00:43:33.409 --> 00:43:36.647
working together to ensure
that these animals are safe.

00:43:50.226 --> 00:43:53.963
ANNOUNCER: Gorillas in the
Mist, the feature film based
on the life of Dian Fossey,

00:43:54.063 --> 00:43:57.368
stars Sigourney Weaver as the
legendary wildlife researcher.

00:44:08.478 --> 00:44:12.749 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
-After I played
Dian and spent so much time
with the Mountain Gorillas in

00:44:13.650 --> 00:44:18.155 line:0%
Rwanda, it was impossible
for me to go back to the
way I saw the world before.

00:44:20.523 --> 00:44:24.861
It was such a gift
to me, actually to be
inside Dian's head.

00:44:25.995 --> 00:44:31.001 align:start size:91% position:9%
I think it was very
frustrating to her that
in the hierarchy of beings

00:44:31.335 --> 00:44:35.605 align:start size:91% position:9%
on the planet,
animals were below humans,
since I think in many ways

00:44:35.705 --> 00:44:38.508 align:start size:78% position:22%
she thought
they were superior.

00:44:39.175 --> 00:44:43.780 align:start position:0%
She felt for a while
like the only person who was
concerned about saving them and

00:44:43.880 --> 00:44:46.450
that was probably true
to a certain extent.

00:44:47.884 --> 00:44:53.357 align:start size:88% position:13%
She knew the movie
would help and I think
she would be so delighted

00:44:54.457 --> 00:44:57.794
and let's not say hopeful,

00:44:57.894 --> 00:45:03.633 align:start size:94% position:6%
but optimistic about
the gorillas' welfare at this
point and even though 880

00:45:03.734 --> 00:45:09.640
still means that the gorillas
are critically endangered,
it's a lot better than 280,

00:45:11.408 --> 00:45:14.411
which it was when she died.

00:45:16.213 --> 00:45:19.449
IAN: It's such a shame
that Dian hasn't lived
to see Mountain Gorillas

00:45:19.549 --> 00:45:21.050
approaching a thousand.

00:45:21.150 --> 00:45:27.624 align:start size:91% position:9%
That is a conservation
success story, which she
would have really enjoyed.

00:45:38.902 --> 00:45:42.706
SIGOURNEY: "I looked
up into Digit's warm,
gentle brown eyes.

00:45:47.277 --> 00:45:52.248 align:start size:94% position:6%
He stood pensively,
gazing down at me before
patting my head and plopping

00:45:52.348 --> 00:45:54.985
down by my side.

00:45:56.253 --> 00:46:01.024 align:start size:88% position:13%
I lay my head on Digit's
lap, a position that
provided welcome warmth.

00:46:06.563 --> 00:46:12.168 align:start size:91% position:9%
When you realize
the value of all life, you
dwell less on what is past

00:46:13.169 --> 00:46:17.541
and concentrate more on the
preservation of the future."

00:46:30.354 --> 00:46:35.692 line:0%
-They're healthy and thriving
and that is Dian's legacy.

00:46:43.033 --> 00:46:46.904 align:start size:91% position:9% line:0%
-Dian, if she were to come
back from the grave, she
would just be so happy.

00:46:49.639 --> 00:46:52.910 line:0%
She did not die in vain.

00:46:57.381 --> 00:47:00.184 line:0%
Her work is continuing
and is going to continue.

00:47:07.891 --> 00:47:09.626 line:0%
Captioned by Cotter
Captioning Services.

